{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":2,"query":"name=Crane&limit=10&title=Latitude","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":[{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":{"title":"Latitude ","subTitle":"the true story of the world's first scientific expedition "},"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Crane, Nicholas","role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author"}}]},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"biography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"History"}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2021"},"copyrightDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2021"},"issuance":"monographic","edition":"First Pegasus books cloth edition."},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York :"}},"agent":{"namePart":"Pegasus Books,","role":{"roleTerm":"publisher"}},"dateIssued":"2021"},{"@eventType":"distribution","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"[New York, New York] :"}},"agent":{"namePart":"Distributed by Simon & Schuster,","role":{"roleTerm":"distributor"}},"dateOther":{"@type":"distribution","#text":"2021."}}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":[{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"257 pages, 16 unnumbered pages of plates : illustrations (some color), maps ; 22 cm"},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"illustration"}},{"form":{"@type":"Color content","#text":"polychrome"}},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"map"}}],"abstract":[{"@type":"Summary","#text":"\"Crane, the former president of the Royal Geographic Society, documents the remarkable expedition undertaken by a group of twelve European adventurer-scientists in the mid-eighteenth century. The team spent years in South America, scaling volcanoes and traversing jungles before they achieved their goal of establishing the exact shape of the Earth by measuring the length of 1 degree latitude at the equator\" Provided by publisher"},{"@type":"Summary","#text":"In 1735 twelve men boarded ships bound for South America. Their mission: to discover the true shape of the earth. Crane documents this expedition to measure one degree latitude at the equator. He shows how their endeavors were not limited to this one achievement: they also discovered rubber and quinine. On a continent of unmapped rainforests and ice-shrouded volcanoes, beset by egos and disease, mutiny and murder, the world's first international team of scientists struggled for a decade to reach the single figure they sought. -- adapted from jacket"}],"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Nicholas Crane."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references (pages 235-245) and index."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":[{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"s------"},{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"s-pe---"}]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Latitude","Measurement","History"],"temporal":"18th century"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Latitude","geographic":"South America"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Scientific expeditions","History"],"geographic":"South America","temporal":"18th century"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Geodesy","Observations","History"],"temporal":"18th century"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Geodesy","geographic":"South America"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Scientific expeditions","geographic":"Peru"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Discoveries in science"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Dis